# --- Cited evidence, and where it lives now -------------------------------------------
# `tmp/` and `logs/` above are scratch-only since 2026-10-16: the 47 tracked files that
# used to sit under them (39 in tmp/, 8 in logs/) moved to `progress/<owner>/evidence/`,
# so `rm -rf tmp/` can no longer delete provenance and nothing here needs `git add -f`.
# Both dirs STAY ignored, precisely because they are now scratch. Evidence files that kept
# a `*.log` name must be re-allowed, because the `*.log` rule above is an unanchored
# directory-independent pattern and bites at any depth (same class as `results/`, `refs/`).
!progress/**/*.log

# --- IDE / OS ---
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
# Prototype build output ONLY, never sources: build.sh writes the binary next to
# its source at prototype/<op>/<op>. A bare `prototype/**/<op>` matches the
# DIRECTORY as well and silently ignores the whole op directory — which is how
# both kernel directories vanished from git with their sources untracked. Name
# the binary path exactly and add one line per new op (or build into
# prototype/<op>/build/, already covered).
prototype/lm_head_gemv/lm_head_gemv
prototype/gdn_decode/gdn_decode
prototype/mlp_gemv/mlp_gemv
prototype/proj_gemv/proj_gemv
prototype/attn_decode/attn_decode
prototype/glue/glue
prototype/gdn_gated_norm/gdn_gated_norm
prototype/gdn_collapse/gdn_collapse_check
prototype/gdn_collapse/neg_*/
prototype/attn_m2/attn_m2
# `build_m16.sh` writes `attn_m16`, or `attn_m16_grp${GRP}` when GRP!=4, next to `attn_m16.hip.cpp`; name the
# outputs exactly (a `prototype/**/attn_m16` pattern would match the directory the source lives in).
prototype/attn_m2/attn_m16
prototype/attn_m2/attn_m16_grp*
prototype/attn_valu_slim/attn_valu_slim
# One line per new op's binary, exact path (the block above explains why a `prototype/**/<op>`
# pattern silently untracks the whole source directory).
prototype/mtp_headbatch/mtp_headbatch
# engine/build.sh writes its binary next to the sources; name the file exactly, never a
# `engine/**/loader_test` pattern (that matches directories — see the block above).
engine/loader_test

# transient compiler/profiler droppings in the repo root
*.hipi
*.hipfb
*.tmp.bc
*hip-amdgcn*
*host-x86_64*
.rocprofv3/

# built binary of the issue-rate probe (the source and gate are tracked; this is the product)
prototype/issue_rate_probe/issue_rate_probe
prototype/gdn_rec_isa/gdn_rec_isa
# same trap, one directory over: the binary is named after its directory, so the path is written in
# full (two components) — `prototype/**/gemm_algo_sweep` would match the directory and hide the sources
prototype/gemm_algo_sweep/gemm_algo_sweep
engines/llama.cpp/
# --save-temps artifacts from a kernel-TU census compile (prototype/attn_wmma/fattn_census_build.sh
# and A10's canary) land in the repo root; the 905 KB listings are regenerable, and the one slice that
# is evidence is tracked under prototype/attn_percost/evidence/. Leading slash so this cannot match a
# directory of the same name (see the trap row about ignore patterns matching op directories).
/kernels_attn-hip-*
/kernels_attn-host-*
prototype/attn_decode_wide/attn_decode_wide
prototype/attn_decode_wide/*.o
prototype/attn_decode_wide/*.s
prototype/attn_decode_wide/*.bc
prototype/attn_decode_wide/*.hipfb
prototype/attn_decode_wide/*.hipi
prototype/attn_decode_wide/*.out
prototype/attn_decode_wide/*.resolution.txt
# mlp_insitu (D2 diagnosis rig): binary named after its directory, so the path is written in
# full — a `prototype/**/mlp_insitu` pattern would match the directory and hide the sources.
prototype/mlp_insitu/mlp_insitu
# gdn_insitu (D4 diagnosis rig): binary named after its directory, so the path is written in
# full — a `prototype/**/gdn_insitu` pattern would match the directory and hide the sources.
prototype/gdn_insitu/gdn_insitu
# s1_launch_price (route S1 gate-zero rig): same trap as above — the binary is named after its
# directory, so the ignore line is the full path, never `prototype/**/s1_launch_price`.
prototype/launch_price/s1_launch_price

# wave_shape (item 2 rig): the binary is named after its directory — ignore the exact path,
# never `prototype/**/wave_shape`, which would match the directory and hide the whole rig (AGENTS trap).
prototype/wave_shape/wave_shape
prototype/wave_shape/out/
# prefetch_tier (route P1 rig + device query): binaries do NOT share the directory name, so these
# exact paths cannot hide the sources — unlike the prototype/<op>/<op> case in the trap row above.
prototype/prefetch_tier/p1c_query
prototype/prefetch_tier/p1_rig
# the timed matrix output; the results belong in a report, not in the tree
prototype/prefetch_tier/out/
# D3 delta rig: raw per-arm rig stdout (the numbers that matter get quoted into
# D3-HANDOVER.md; components.py reads this directory, so it is regenerable, not source)
prototype/mtp_delta/evidence/
